model {
  extend basalt.build {
    metadata {
      constraint "When CI provides the emulate CLI, a local Cloud runs its sign-in, mail, company and directory stand-ins in one emulator process of its own on loopback, beside the billing one, and keys each at the service's root instead of creating a hosted instance. A stage signing in through another Cloud shares that Cloud's services. Without the CLI every service stays hosted, as before. Emulator ports come from below the OS's ephemeral range, where the Cloud, its runtime and Docker never get theirs, and concurrent starts reserve each port exclusively for their scope, so no other process in the stack can be given one; a bind that still fails is reported, never retried. Where the sign-in stand-in is on loopback the Cloud SSO test has no public issuer: it asserts the stand-in is refused like any private issuer and declares the public-issuer registration not proved, which a unit test at the SSO library's discovery seam proves instead."
    }
  }
}
